  "authoritative_metadata": "manifest.json",
  "title": "A cross-layer hard pair makes counting #P-hard although the class-2 quotient is easy",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "for p >= 5, r | p - 1 and a graded Lie algebra L1 + L2 + L3 over F_p of class at most 3 with a coprime split C_r action (a group of exponent p through the Lazard correspondence), homomorphisms over a character are layered crossed homomorphisms f1 + f2 + f3 with d f2 = -(1/2) f1 u f1 and d f3 = -R(f1, f2), R = (1/2)(f1 u f2 + f2 u f1) + (1/12) C(f1); the count depends only on cohomology classes, and on manifolds with H1 = Z/r the trivial-character parts drop out. For the free class-3 group on x (trivial character) and y (character alpha, alpha^2 != 1), on every such manifold and in every sector the count is |Z1(F_alpha^k)| times the Heisenberg (alpha, alpha) count, so counting maps from pi1 of r-surgeries on knots to it is #P-hard (CLASSK-DICHOTOMY-20261026-001C), although its class-2 quotient has no hard pair and is polynomial with bounded homology (COPRIME-CLASS2-20261026-001C).",
