    "A BCH group that fails associativity, exponent p or equivariance on sampled elements.",
    "A knot surgery and sector on which the layered direct lifting count (cocycles, then the affine layer-2 and layer-3 systems by the group law) differs from the class-dependent formula.",
    "A knot surgery and sector on which the cross-layer group's count differs from |Z1(F_alpha^k)| times the Heisenberg (alpha, alpha) count.",
    "A cross-layer group whose class-2 quotient has a hard pair, or a Heisenberg (alpha, alpha) sector-1 weight that is constant on its gadget model.",
    "A control that cannot fail: with alpha^2 = 1 the cross-layer count must be independent of the cup products."
